capability html/format  a tree written as HTML by the standard's serialisation
  heroes  html.format, html.format_node, html.format_inner
  go      x/net/html: Render
  rust    -
  python  str(Tag), Tag.decode, Tag.decode_contents, Tag.encode, html5lib.serialize, html5lib HTMLSerializer
  note    the standard's algorithm: `&`, a no-break space, `<` and `>` escaped in text and values, `"` in values, void elements with no end tag, raw text kept. Go's Render writes `<br/>` and escapes otherwise; BeautifulSoup writes `<br/>` too. Bytes are `strings.to_bytes`, a stream `io`

